---
import PostLayout from "../../../components/PostLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

export const meta = {
    title: "Music at hack4play with strudel.cc",
    date: new Date(2026, 1, 22),
    description:
        "Workshop notes from Kochi Bienalle's Forplay Society programme",
    tags: ["music"],
};
---

<PostLayout meta={meta}>
    <p>
        The following are notes from my workshop at the Kochi Bienalle
        Collateral Programme, Forplay Society.
    </p><p>
        Use <a href="/posts/20250924-music-at-indiafoss-with-strudelcc"
            >my talk at IndiaFOSS last year</a
        > as a reference.
    </p><ol>
        <li>What kind of music do you listen to?</li>
        <li>What programming experience do you have? Does it matter?</li>
        <li>What do you expect to leave with after this workshop?</li>
        <li>
            Do we have time to jam? Use flok locally <code
                >pnpx flok-web@1.3.0</code
            > if we get the time.
        </li>
    </ol><h2>Should we turn this sad tune to upbeat dance music?</h2><ol>
        <li>What is that <code>initHydra()</code>?</li>
    </ol>
    <iframe
        src="https://strudel.cc/#c2V0Y3BtKDYwKQogIApsZXQgY2hvcmRzID0gY2hvcmQoIjxBbSBENyA8R003IENNNyBbR2FkZDksIENNN10%"
        width="100%"
        height="500"
    ></iframe><h2>Samples 101</h2>
    <iframe
        src="https://strudel.cc/#%3D"
        width="100%"
        height="500"
    ></iframe><h2>Samples again (?)</h2>
    <iframe
        src="https://strudel.cc/#%3D%3D"
        width="100%"
        height="500"
    ></iframe><h2>Try some of these</h2>
    <Code lang="text" code={`$: s("bd bd cp@2")`} />
    <Code lang="text" code={`$: s("bd hh bd hh")`} />
    <Code
        lang="text"
        code={`_$: s("bd*4\\)
_$: s("hh*8")
_$: ("~ sd")`}
    />
    <Code
        lang="text"
        code={`$: s("bd sd [~ bd] sd, hh*6").bank("RolandTR909")`}
    /><h2>Glossary</h2><blockquote>
        <p>
            To set a specific bpm, use <code>setcpm(bpm/bpc)</code> bpm: the
            target beats per minute, bpc: the number of perceived beats per
            cycle. <code>setcpm(110/4) s("bd sd bd rim, hh*8")</code> could
            be interpreted as 4/4 time with a tempo of 110bpm.
        </p>
    </blockquote><blockquote>
        <p>
            Tempo is based on perception. The choice of sounds also has an
            impact on the tempo feel. This is why the same CPM can produce
            different perceived tempos.
        </p>
    </blockquote><blockquote>
        <p>
            Playing more than one note at a time is generally called a <code
                >chord</code
            >. Notes are discernible sounds.
        </p>
    </blockquote><blockquote>
        <p>
            Slow down using <code>/</code>, Alternate using <code
                >&lt;&gt;</code
            >, Elongate using <code>@</code>, Replicate using <code
                >!</code
            >, Parallel using <code>,</code>, Speed up using <code
                >*</code
            >, Sub-sequence using <code>[]</code>, Rest using <code
                >~</code
            >.
        </p>
    </blockquote><blockquote>
        <p>Filters help shape a sound</p>
    </blockquote><blockquote>
        <p>
            <code>bd</code> = <strong>b</strong>ass <strong>d</strong>rum, <code
                >sd</code
            > = <strong>s</strong>nare <strong>d</strong>rum, <code
                >rim</code
            > = <strong>rim</strong>shot, <code>hh</code> = <strong
                >h</strong
            >i<strong>h</strong>at, <code>oh</code> = <strong>o</strong>pen <strong
                >h</strong
            >ihat, <code>lt</code> = <strong>l</strong>ow tom, <code
                >mt</code
            > = <strong>m</strong>iddle tom, <code>ht</code> = <strong
                >h</strong
            >igh tom, <code>rd</code> = <strong>r</strong>i<strong
                >d</strong
            >e cymbal, <code>cr</code> = <strong>cr</strong>ash cymbal, <code
                >cp</code
            > = <strong>c</strong>la<strong>p</strong>
        </p>
    </blockquote>
</PostLayout>
